  <channel>
    <title>InvestPR Media Monitoring</title>
    <link>https://bestedc.github.io/ipr-digest-feed/digest.xml</link>
    <description>Two concrete investment items lead the period: Claro will spend $35 million on a second AMX-1 submarine-cable landing station, adding redundancy to Puerto Rico's international data routes and reducing hurricane and equipment-failure outage risk, and the Energy Bureau approved a 20-year storage agreement between PREPA and Yabucoa Energy for a 100 MW/400 MWh battery on the former Shell refinery site, with a $20 million cap on interconnection costs that cannot be passed to ratepayers. Both are infrastructure signals that speak directly to the reliability concerns site-selection consultants raise about the island. On the policy side, the Centro Unido de Detallistas renewed pressure to eliminate the inventory tax and speed permitting reform, framing permit delays as a hidden tax on business — advocacy rather than action, but a persistent competitiveness theme.</description>
    <language>en-us</language>
    <lastBuildDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 03:15:42 +0000</lastBuildDate>
